Z||000015||1FST2M6||10-03-2001||08:55 AM||||yep the dyno rollers weight 3600lbs.. my car tips the scales at well under that.  the computer and sensors that are hooked to both the car (ignition) and the dyno roller take into account the weight and time... the rolling resistance and wind difference are offset by the additional weight of the drums over that of my car.  my car hooks up better on the street so i'm sure that 4.91 is more than adequit.. i can pull 0-84 in 8.1 with plenty of tire spin... (at the 1/8mi track and 0-109 in 12.9 at the 1/4mi track)<P><BR>the BOOM on the dyno... OOH good grief!  ok.. i told Ed (driver in video - and dyno tuner) i wanted a 0-? run off idle sprayin. he was all "i don't think thats a good idea" well after explaining to him that how i run the car any way -off idle pedal to the floor nitrous flowing- and it's been fien for the SE and now 9+ bottles on the GT it'll be fine this time too... well he still being leary power brakes it to 1500rpm on the dyno hits the dyno logging switch and lays on the throttle.... 9 seconds later JUST into 3rd the wet system shows it's ugly side... the unburnt fuel had puddled in the exhaust before the cat and <B>BOOOM</B> sending Ed into the floor of the car... my bro-in-law crapping his pants and me to for a second.. untill we realized that there were no falling parts and that it was just a back fire not a spectacular parts flying failure. that was the last run of the morning. i chickened out of my changes... I messed with the fuel jetting and ed screwed with the s-afc... now it pulls like a train!!! i had it WAY pig rich at 9.5:1 air fuel when we irst straped it down.. we leaned it way out and it's still TOO rich at the upper RPM range.. time for a 2nd stage nitrous only jet... i'll keep everyone posted... <P><BR>----- dyno movie descriptions...<BR>22 - baseline movie before fuel tuning<BR>23 - about the 15 second mark the nitrous is turned on.. 2.46 seconds later 2nd gear is over<BR>BOOM- the 0-60 run after fuel tuning but it loaded up in the exhaust and BOOM! (backfired) scared us all for about 2 seconds.. then we realized there was no falling debris and i took the car off the dyno.. ... yep i wussed out. <P><BR>thanks a TON for hosting those!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> mind if i send the link to a few others?!<P><BR>------------------<BR>0-60 in 4.91<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||jimmybpei||10-03-2001||07:28 PM||||Travis,<P>Thanks a lot for the info. Is there jets available to get this up to about 150hp shot.<P>My bottom end is done and bolted.<BR>Topend. heads are ported and polished headers<BR>, holley 255l/hr fuel pump, adj. fuel pressure regulator & guage, cold air kit, <BR>msd 6al box msd coil wires plugs. plan on getting a bored throttle and plenium from Dave M???. <P>My car is an auto with a shift kit. thinking on putting in a 85 4 speed Y/N ?<P>Anything else i might need. Fule delivery, ignition and air. Think it' all covered????<P>Thanks<BR>Jimmy B.<P>||||reg||1
